* BEHAVIOURAL OPA2197 AND INA828 for the system deck, from their banked datasheets, each
* parameter a sims.yaml param with its page. TI's macromodels are what every other sim in
* this repository uses, and they are banked here too (models:); in this deck they find no
* DC operating point and stall a cold start at random corners (README, "Why behavioural"),
* so this directory's own sims hold these blocks to TI's models where it matters: PSRR
* and CMRR against frequency (sims opamp-check and inamp-check).
*
* BOPA, one OPA2197 channel: pins in+ in- V+ V- out.
*  - the supply's error, input-referred: ps_k0 per volt of (V+ - V-) away from ps_vs0, and a
*    derivative term ps_tau, the 20 dB/decade TI's model shows above ~10 Hz
*  - a transconductance stage, slew-limited (i_slew = SR x cx), into rx || cx about the
*    supplies' midpoint: Aol = gm rx, GBW = gm / (2 pi cx)
*  - the integrator clamped inside the rails (rail-to-rail output, v_hr from each)
*  - a push-pull output from the rails themselves, r_o open loop (opa2197-output-impedance),
*    limited at i_sc, alive only while the supply is (so an unpowered amplifier sources
*    nothing): its load current is drawn from V+ or returned to V-, as a real output stage's
*  - its quiescent current from V+ to V-, smoothly zero at zero supply
.subckt BOPA inp inn vcc vee out
Bmid mid 0 V = 0.5 * (V(vcc) + V(vee))
Bps eps 0 V = {{ps_k0}} * (V(vcc) - V(vee) - {{ps_vs0}}) + {{ps_tau}} * ddt(V(vcc) - V(vee))
Bgm mid x I = {{i_slew}} * tanh({{gm_op}} * (V(inp) - V(inn) + V(eps)) / {{i_slew}})
Rx x mid {{rx_op}}
Cx x mid {{cx_op}}
Bxh xh 0 V = V(vcc) - {{v_hr}}
Bxl xl 0 V = V(vee) + {{v_hr}}
Dxh x xh DLIMOP
Dxl xl x DLIMOP
Bal al 0 V = 0.5 * (1 + tanh((V(vcc) - V(vee) - 2) / 0.5))
Bio io 0 V = {{i_sc}} * tanh((V(x) - V(out)) / ({{i_sc}} * {{r_o}})) * V(al)
Bsrc vcc out I = 0.5 * (V(io) + sqrt(V(io) * V(io) + 1e-14))
Bsnk out vee I = 0.5 * (sqrt(V(io) * V(io) + 1e-14) - V(io))
Bq vcc vee I = {{iq_op}} * tanh((V(vcc) - V(vee)) / 2)
.model DLIMOP D(Is=1e-14 N=1)
.ends
*
* BINA, the INA828: its datasheet's three-amplifier topology [INA828IDR.pdf, Functional
* Block Diagram]: two input amplifiers with their 25 kohm feedback and RG between their
* inverting inputs (G = 1 + 50 kohm / RG, so the netlist's R-GAIN-INAMP sets it), and a
* difference amplifier of four 40 kohm resistors to OUT and REF. Its CMRR is a mismatch,
* ina_d in the REF leg (the datasheet's minimum at dc), and a capacitance across it,
* ina_cm (the roll-off TI's model shows). Pins: in+ in- V+ V- out ref rg1 rg2.
.subckt BINA inp inn vcc vee out ref rg1 rg2
XA1 inn rg1 vcc vee a1 BOPA
RF1 a1 rg1 25k
XA2 inp rg2 vcc vee a2 BOPA
RF2 a2 rg2 25k
R3 a1 n3 40k
R4 n3 out 40k
R5 a2 p3 40k
R6 p3 ref {{r_ina_ref}}
C6 p3 ref {{ina_cm}}
XA3 p3 n3 vcc vee out BOPA
.ends
